Matplotlib — Graphs and Visualization 📈

Matplotlib is used to show your data visually.

For example:

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

x = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
y = [10, 20, 15, 30, 25]

plt.plot(x, y)

plt.show()

===

It creates a line graph.

You can create:

Line charts
Bar charts
Scatter plots
Histograms
Pie charts

Example:

plt.bar(x, y)
plt.show()
Think:

Matplotlib = Make graphs from data

====
